{"type":"standard","title":"Bobby Pulido","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Bobby Pulido</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3297865","titles":{"canonical":"Bobby_Pulido","normalized":"Bobby Pulido","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Bobby Pulido</span></span>"},"pageid":546023,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Bobby_Pulido_%28CROPPED%29.jpg/330px-Bobby_Pulido_%28CROPPED%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":423},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/Bobby_Pulido_%28CROPPED%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":533,"height":683},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378087729","tid":"5af8bbd6-beaf-11f1-9e46-545b9e90f283","timestamp":"2026-10-02T22:19:38Z","description":"American singer (born 1973)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobby_Pulido","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobby_Pulido?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobby_Pulido?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Bobby_Pulido"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobby_Pulido","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Bobby_Pulido","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobby_Pulido?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Bobby_Pulido"}},"extract":"José Roberto Pulido Jr. is an American singer, songwriter, guitarist, actor, and political candidate. He is credited with expanding the audience for Tejano music among younger listeners, emerging as a teen idol among Mexican-American teenagers in the 1990s and becoming one of Tejano music's most prominent recording artists.","extract_html":"<p><b>José Roberto Pulido Jr.</b> is an American singer, songwriter, guitarist, actor, and political candidate. He is credited with expanding the audience for Tejano music among younger listeners, emerging as a teen idol among Mexican-American teenagers in the 1990s and becoming one of Tejano music's most prominent recording artists.</p>"}